# r107e_caustics-puddles: FEATURE follow-up to r107d_caustics-lamp-look.py (applies ON TOP of r107,
# r107b, r107c and r107d; branch when published: visual/glass-water). Context:
# bbfss-ctx-glass-water-caustics.md, section "2026-11-15 r107e".
#
# r107d (batch b19) settled it: the model's units are right (0.58-0.70 of the pixel near the
# lantern), the sewer's light where its caustics land is not the lantern's, and even the look at 4
# shows nothing there. The lead's decision: puddles as water for the lamp caustics.
#  - In frames without a mirrored water pass (after 16 such calls), with BB_CAUSTICS_LAMPS set,
#    every G-buffer pass counts the puddle candidates (normal from the depth facing up, world y
#    >= 0.9; G-buffer gloss >= 0.8) by height under the camera (128 steps of 4 cm). The host takes
#    the plane from the dispatch read 7 later (EstimatePuddle: the most crowded 3 steps, enough
#    candidates, half of them within 8 cm), hands it to the next passes, and uses it for lamps once
#    the guard has read it: at most 0.6 of the up-facing pixels on it are candidates (a glossy dry
#    floor is refused).
#  - A lamp's crossing is water only on a candidate pixel on that plane; hidden crossings never
#    count there; the pattern on a puddle drifts at 0.25 of the speed with half the contrast.
#  - Log: "Water caustics (r107e)".
#
# Files: r107's own only (host_shaders/caustics.comp, caustics_layout.h; renderer_vulkan/
# caustics_params.h, vk_caustics.h, vk_caustics.cpp; tests/test_caustics.cpp; README.md: r107's
# paragraph and two rows). Counter slots 32 -> 168 words (buffer 2560 -> 6912 bytes). No new file,
# no new binding.
#
# Off (BB_CAUSTICS and BB_CAUSTICS_LAMPS unset): as r107: the rasterizer makes no Caustics.
#
# Use: python -I -X utf8 r107e_caustics-puddles.py check | apply | revert. Root from R107E_ROOT,
# R107D_ROOT, R107C_ROOT, R107B_ROOT or R107_ROOT, else <tree>. Each edit is an exact text
# (old -> new) found exactly once; "applied" = every new text once and its old one gone, "clean" =
# every old text once and no new one; anything else is refused (exit 1, nothing written). Line ends
# are kept (CRLF in the tree). apply keeps the touched files in r107e_backup/ next to this script.
# Revert order: r107e, r107d, r107c, r107b, r107 (the older scripts' checks fail on r107e's slots).
# Exit: 0 done, 1 refused, 2 usage.
